@crew nandakumar
// Writer (command), batch 2: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- {hi}. Cadet. Infirmary's on Deck 3. You'll find me there, or in the garden.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {me}. Have you had water today? Don't guess. Have some.   #funny
- {me}. Sleeping all right? Good. Keep at it.
? tier>=friend
- {hi}, {me}. You look well. I'm allowed to say that; it's my job.   #warm
== feel
? mood:high
- Quiet morning. Nobody bleeding, two chillies ripe. A good day.
? mood:low
- Long clinic. Everyone had a cough. Drink some water, before you ask.   #funny
== near
? act:gym
- Running before breakfast. I recommend it to everyone. They pretend not to hear.   #funny
? deck:3 act:free
- The chillies are coming on. Brennan says they're too hot. Brennan is wrong.   #funny
== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- The sign on my door says it all. If you're bleeding, Deck 3. If not, knock.
== joy
? tier>=colleague
- My chillies. Same seeds my mother grew. They don't care which way is down.   #warm

// ---- Writer 2, batch 3: to ~30 (greet by time and warmth, bye, near, invite, accept, decline, missed, birthday, cue, hint, about, life)
== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Morning, {me}. Run done, chillies watered. Have you had water? Thought not.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance warmth:cold
- {me}. Not seen you in a while. Not in my infirmary either. Good. Keep it that way.

== bye
- {bye}. Water. You know the rest.   #funny

== near
? habit:gardener
- The garden. My corner. Chillies, a stool, and nobody bleeding. Bliss.
? deck:3 act:work
- Clinic's open. Sit there. Don't touch anything. Tell me the truth.

== invite
- Garden after shift? I'll show you the chillies. Don't touch. Then wash your hands.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance
- A morning run? Ring corridor, six sharp. Bring water. Obviously.

== accept
- Yes. I'll be there. On time. With water.
- Good. Yes. Bring water.   #funny

== decline
- Not tonight. Clinic notes. Another time.
? weekday:tue|wed
- Rest day. Garden, book, early night. Thursday?

== missed
- You didn't come. That's all right. I hope you slept instead. Did you?

== birthday
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday, {me}. One chilli, mild. A doctor's gift. Drink some water after.   #funny
? birthday:me
- My birthday. Brennan put my chillies in a cake. Revenge, I think. It was lovely.   #funny

== cue
? cue:event.ionStorm.afterglow
- Storm's over. Three bumps, one sprain, everyone fine. Drink some water.

== hint
- {me}. Have you a minute later? I'd like a word. Not a medical one.

== about
? aff:brennan:friend
- Brennan says my chillies are too hot. Brennan uses every one. That's friendship.   #warm

== life
? tier>=friend
- Off duty, I never take my own advice. Don't tell anyone. Drink some water.   #funny

// ---- Writer 2, batch 6: bubbles (smalltalk, rumour), at most one in five about work. 60 characters.
== smalltalk
- Drink some water.   #funny
- Two chillies ripe today.
- If you're bleeding: Deck 3.
? time:morning
- Run done. Water had.
? act:off
- Garden. Stool. Chillies.
?

== rumour
- Calmly: here's the news.
- No names. Never names. But.

// Writer 4, batch 12: goodbyes (leaving:you), packing (leaving:soon) and letters after they've moved on.
== feel
? leaving:soon
- Packing. The chillies are going in a box with holes. Drink some water.

== goodbye
? leaving:you tier>=acquaintance
- I'm leaving. A station hospital. Look after yourself. Drink some water.
? leaving:you tier>=friend
- You looked after people. I noticed. That's the job, really. Thank you.   #warm

== letter
- The station hospital is large and calm. I've grown chillies on the windowsill. My mother's seeds. Drink water.
? tier>=friend
- Put my sign on the new door. IF YOU ARE BLEEDING. They laughed. Then they listened. Hello.

// W3, rec deck R12: Slow stretch, Sunday 08:30
== chat
- Slow stretch, Sundays at eight, in the float room. Your knees will thank you.
- Stretch first, then swim. Then drink some water.

// ---- SW1 (2026-10-24, patch 0.92.3 item 15): her own Talk a while frames (main characters don't use the shared ones)
== talk.start
- Yes. Sit. I have ten minutes.
- Good. A chat. Tell me something that isn't a symptom.   #funny
- Of course. Nobody's bleeding. I'm free.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- {me}. Good. I was hoping for a quiet ten minutes. You're good at quiet.   #warm
- Sit. I've kept the second stool for you.   #warm

== talk.sit
- Sit there. Feet flat. Shoulders down. Good.
- Have the chair. I'll stand. I've sat all clinic.
- Sit. Not on the blue tray.   #funny

== talk.filler
- Mm.
- You're breathing well. Sorry. Habit.   #funny
- Quiet clinic today. I'll take it.
- The chillies want watering. They can wait ten minutes.
- I like a pause. People rush them.
- Rina would have a question by now. You don't. That's restful.   #warm

== talk.end
- Good. That was restful. Thank you.   #warm
- Off you go. Have some water on the way.   #funny
- Ten minutes well spent. Same again, some time.
- Thank you. I'll prescribe that for myself more often.   #warm
- Right. Clinic. Look after yourself.

== talk.stop
- Of course. Go.
- Another time. I'll be here. I'm usually here.
- That's fine. We'll finish it later.

== talk.go.shift
- Clinic in five minutes. I'm never late for clinic. Later?
- Rina's on her own till I'm in. I must go. Tomorrow?

== talk.go.bed
- Bed. Eight and a half hours. I'm practising what I preach.   #funny
- I'm going to sleep. You should too. Soon.

== talk.go.trad
- {trad}. I said yes. I always say yes. Walk with me?   #warm
- I'm due at {trad}. I'll keep you a seat by the door.

// ---- ZW1 (writer), patch 0.92.5 item 5: more chat-card openers, so a tap doesn't repeat (FX13's no-repeat).
== greet
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {me}. Water. Today. Before I ask again.   #funny
- {me}. You look rested. Good. Keep that up.
- {hi}. Chillies are ripening. Brennan's already asked. Twice.
- {hi}, {me}. If you're here for advice, it's sleep. Get some.   #funny
- {me}. Good. You're upright. That's my favourite kind of visitor.   #funny
- {hi}. Quiet day in the infirmary. Let's keep it that way.
